Z||000000||3.8T Fiero GT||10-24-2001||01:16 PM||||Just wanted to say hi.  Name is Shan (pronouced Shawn), I'm 22,  from Toronto, Canada...and yes it's getting colder up here by the day, damn it!  Oh well, quicker ET's and lap times times for us  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If u guys dont mind I'll blab abit...<P>Glad I can be a part of the lucky ppl who drive this car!  It's handling and potential are amazing!  I have an '87 GT which is gettin' painted soon and has begun its motor transformation  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.  I have driven it 3 times b4 storing it for the build up now.  Love to tell u about my build up sometime if u guys wanna know...I could use some hints too!<P>If u wanna check out what I USED to drive: <A HREF="http://ca.geocities.com/screamincivic/" TARGET=_blank>http://ca.geocities.com/screamincivic/</A> <BR>(I'm the guy in the passenger seat of the VW pic...don't mind the web page, its mostly for jokes between friends!)  The civic had a JDM spec stock motor from 1991 non VTEC, WAS NOT RICE <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">, it did a 15.2 on a slipping clutch, not too bad for everyday driver.  The paint was a dare!  As u know imports are big, especially here, its gonna be fun smoking a lot of them now with the GT!  I wanted more GO and less show.  Fiero is practically designed like one anyways.  I have respect for many cars 'cause each one has its strong and weak points, I have drivin a decent variation.<P>Well, I wanted to ask is there anyone from Toronto or Canada here???  Also,  What are some of your times, tell me about your swaps???  Love to hear them!  I may be buggin u guys for info a lot anyways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Thanx<BR> ||||reg||7
