Z||000010||lildevil||10-24-2001||06:49 PM||||welcome to the forum.  Its good to see a young trying to customize something other then a Civic these days.  The main reason i stuck with mine through the years is cause its different.  As for your conversion...I'd say mid 12's would be realistic with the boost turned up.  Mine runs 13.2's so far with 9 pounds of boost.  With 16 you could easily be in the mid to low twelves.  Mine is the supercharged version by the way and its a auto.  Go to <A HREF="http://www.cwest.com." TARGET=_blank>www.cwest.com.</A>  They jus did a 3800 turbo. You could ask them for some numbers and advice.<P><P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||3.8T Fiero GT||10-24-2001||08:28 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Welcome to the forum, I am from burlington Ontario there is a whole lot of us from around here, my apt building we have 3 people, BanditBalz, myself, and one other non forum guy, we have a 87 GT silver (mine), a 86GT Silver (BanditBalz) and a 88T-Top.<P>Check out my website if you have a chance.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Thanks all of you.<P>Hey grint, nice page, not too far from me. i LOVE the old school Need For Speed music, now u need his voice over too! lol.  Nortel networks huh...hmm, i am almost done studying IT @ York U this year...hope u dont mind if i start hounding u for an IT job in a year or so?? haha   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>72vinman-haha, sounds tempting...actually my bestfriend/mechanic does most of the work!  I help with what i can.  we'll see how easy (OR HARD) it is and let u know..ya never know, just have enuff saved to buy the parts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>lildevil-thanks, i know what u mean about "civics" and all, well i know my cars...glad u can see that SOME of us youngins know a cars worth when they see it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  civics, well they have there fun side, i have been overseas a couple of times and they are more impressive there than the ones here!  I read up on all cars, domestic to imports...i must say i love my camaros and vettes..and fieros of course!, but man, I REALLY LOVE some of the amazing imports that we dont even get here!!! Jap and euro alike!!! As for the tims...wicked, thats what i am hoping for!  i know about CWEST, i will check it up as i havent been to the site for quite a while!  u got my mind going again <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">...i am hoping to run 20 pounds as the turbo can handle upwards of 30, but the motor can only take su much...<BR>